<article class="mx-auto max-w-5xl py-10 sm:py-14">
  <header class="rounded-3xl border border-apx-line bg-apx-surface p-6 sm:p-10">
    <p class="apx-mono-label">About APX</p>
    <h1 class="mt-4 max-w-4xl text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-apx-text sm:text-5xl">
      Sovereign Policy Analytics &amp; Expert Consensus Engine
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-6 max-w-3xl text-xl leading-8 text-apx-muted">
      APX organizes source-linked claims, policy proposals, attributed positions, voting signals,
      and intelligence briefs so people can inspect the evidence and the limits of each conclusion.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-7 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
      <.link
        href={~p"/explore"}
        class="rounded-lg bg-apx-blue px-5 py-3 font-semibold text-white hover:brightness-110"
      >Explore proposals</.link>
      <.link
        href={~p"/intelligence"}
        class="rounded-lg border border-apx-cyan px-5 py-3 font-semibold text-apx-cyan hover:bg-apx-cyan/10"
      >Open intelligence</.link>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section aria-labelledby="about-method" class="py-12">
    <h2 id="about-method" class="text-2xl font-bold text-apx-text">A source-first method</h2>
    <div class="mt-6 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2">
      <div class="apx-panel p-6">
        <p class="apx-mono-label">Evidence layer</p>
        <h3 class="mt-2 text-xl font-semibold text-apx-text">Traceable public positions</h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-apx-muted">
          Quotes and claims can be linked to authors, dates, original sources, and the policy
          proposals they bear on. Verification states describe individual checks; they do not
          guarantee truth or eliminate context disputes.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="apx-panel p-6">
        <p class="apx-mono-label">Participation layer</p>
        <h3 class="mt-2 text-xl font-semibold text-apx-text">Direct voting and optional delegation</h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-apx-muted">
          Participants may vote directly or delegate to people they trust. Direct votes take
          precedence; delegated results are derived from the selected delegates' recorded votes.
          Participation is not automatically representative of the public or of technical experts.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="about-language" class="border-t border-apx-line py-12">
    <h2 id="about-language" class="text-2xl font-bold text-apx-text">How to read APX signals</h2>
    <div class="mt-6 space-y-4">
      <div class="apx-panel p-6">
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-apx-text">Empirical Consensus Metrics</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-apx-muted">
          APX surfaces recorded positions and disagreement. It does not invent a consensus
          percentage or claim that a self-selected group represents all experts.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="apx-panel p-6">
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-apx-text">Non-Deterministic System Verification</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-apx-muted">
          Automated and human review can disagree. A status indicates what a particular check found,
          with source links available for readers to reassess the item.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="apx-panel p-6">
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-apx-text">Sovereign Telemetry</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-apx-muted">
          The <.link href={~p"/intelligence"} class="text-apx-cyan underline">intelligence hub</.link>
          monitors high-authority public feeds. Its impact labels are rule-based triage of headlines
          and RSS excerpts—not official threat assessments or full-article analysis.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="about-audience" class="border-t border-apx-line py-12">
    <h2 id="about-audience" class="text-2xl font-bold text-apx-text">Designed for public scrutiny</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl leading-7 text-apx-muted">
      APX is intended to support researchers, parliamentarians, committee clerks, journalists, and
      sovereign security leads who need to examine policy arguments and their sources. This describes
      the intended audience, not an endorsement or current adoption claim.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl leading-7 text-apx-muted">
      APX is a policy analytics project. It is not currently a registered non-profit institute,
      government service, official technical standard, or certification authority. No claim is made
      that its current participants amount to a fixed share of independent auditors or policy
      fellows.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="about-boundaries" class="rounded-2xl border border-apx-line bg-[#0D1421] p-6 sm:p-8">
    <h2 id="about-boundaries" class="text-xl font-bold text-apx-text">What APX does not decide</h2>
    <ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-sm leading-6 text-apx-muted">
      <li>It does not determine whether a claim is true solely from a vote or popularity measure.</li>
      <li>It does not bind governments, companies, or the people whose views are recorded.</li>
      <li>It does not infer that a quoted public figure has personally cast a vote on APX.</li>
      <li>Its AI-assisted checks and RSS triage can be incomplete or wrong; primary sources remain essential.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="about-participate" class="border-t border-apx-line pt-10">
    <h2 id="about-participate" class="text-2xl font-bold text-apx-text">Help improve the record</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-7 text-apx-muted">
      Bring a missing source, a well-supported objection, or a question that deserves closer
      examination. Review the
      <.link href={~p"/dataset"} class="font-semibold text-apx-cyan underline">public dataset</.link>
      or contact the project through the contact form.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-5 font-semibold text-apx-cyan">
      <.link href={~p"/explore"} class="underline underline-offset-4">Explore proposals</.link>
      <.link :if={!@current_user} href={~p"/sign_up"} class="underline underline-offset-4">Join APX</.link>
      <.link href={~p"/contact"} class="underline underline-offset-4">Contact</.link>
      <.link href={~p"/faq"} class="underline underline-offset-4">Frequently asked questions</.link>
    </div>
  </section>
</article>
